{"uid":"415eb06f563e89b9","name":"test_the_ruff_pin_in_ci_matches_the_one_developers_install","fullName":"tests.test_ci_local_parity#test_the_ruff_pin_in_ci_matches_the_one_developers_install","historyId":"1ee269072404b940437eb08c8b9b14d2","time":{"start":1792080507307,"stop":1792080507309,"duration":2},"description":"A version skew here fails CI on files the author never touched.\n\n    ruff's formatter output shifts between releases, so a developer whose venv\n    resolved a newer ruff formats a file the way *their* version wants, and CI's\n    pinned version rejects it. The diff then points at unrelated files, which is\n    the least useful possible signal -- and it happened: a local ruff 0.16.1\n    disagreed with CI's 0.15.20 on three files nobody had edited.\n\n    Both pins are asserted equal so bumping one alone is a test failure rather\n    than a confusing CI failure later.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>A version skew here fails CI on files the author never touched.</p>\n<pre><code>ruff's formatter output shifts between releases, so a developer whose venv\nresolved a newer ruff formats a file the way *their* version wants, and CI's\npinned version rejects it. The diff then points at unrelated files, which is\nthe least useful possible signal -- and it happened: a local ruff 0.16.1\ndisagreed with CI's 0.15.20 on three files nobody had edited.\n\nBoth pins are asserted equal so bumping one alone is a test failure rather\nthan a confusing CI failure later.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"failed","statusMessage":"AssertionError: ruff pin drifted: CI installs ['0.16.6'], dev extras install ['0.17.0']\nassert {'0.16.6'} == {'0.17.0'}\n  \n  Extra items in the left set:\n  '0.16.6'\n  Extra items in the right set:\n  '0.17.0'\n  \n  Full diff:\n    {\n  -     '0.17.0',\n  ?         ^ ^\n  +     '0.16.6',\n  ?         ^ ^\n    }","statusTrace":"def test_the_ruff_pin_in_ci_matches_the_one_developers_install() -> None:\n        \"\"\"A version skew here fails CI on files the author never touched.\n    \n        ruff's formatter output shifts between releases, so a developer whose venv\n        resolved a newer ruff formats a file the way *their* version wants, and CI's\n        pinned version rejects it. The diff then points at unrelated files, which is\n        the least useful possible signal -- and it happened: a local ruff 0.16.1\n        disagreed with CI's 0.15.20 on three files nobody had edited.\n    \n        Both pins are asserted equal so bumping one alone is a test failure rather\n        than a confusing CI failure later.\n        \"\"\"\n        workflow = (REPO_ROOT / \".github\" / \"workflows\" / \"ci.yml\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        ci_pins = re.findall(r'ruff==([0-9][^\"\\'\\s]*)', workflow)\n        assert ci_pins, \"the CI lint job no longer pins ruff to an exact version\"\n    \n        pyproject = (REPO_ROOT / \"caliber\" / \"pyproject.toml\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        dev_pins = re.findall(r'\"ruff==([0-9][^\"]*)\"', pyproject)\n        assert dev_pins, (\n            \"caliber's dev extras no longer pin ruff exactly; a developer venv would \"\n            \"be free to resolve a version whose formatter disagrees with CI's\"\n        )\n    \n>       assert set(ci_pins) == set(dev_pins), (\n            f\"ruff pin drifted: CI installs {sorted(set(ci_pins))}, \"\n            f\"dev extras install {sorted(set(dev_pins))}\"\n        )\nE       AssertionError: ruff pin drifted: CI installs ['0.16.6'], dev extras install ['0.17.0']\nE       assert {'0.16.6'} == {'0.17.0'}\nE         \nE         Extra items in the left set:\nE         '0.16.6'\nE         Extra items in the right set:\nE         '0.17.0'\nE         \nE         Full diff:\nE           {\nE         -     '0.17.0',\nE         ?         ^ ^\nE         +     '0.16.6',\nE         ?         ^ ^\nE           }\n\ntests/test_ci_local_parity.py:239: AssertionError","flaky":false,"newFailed":true,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"r